{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Speak to Aaron and to his sons, saying: Thus shall you bless</b> – I have already mentioned in the portion of \"And it came to pass on the eighth day\" (Leviticus 9:22) that He commanded Aaron to lift his hands toward the people and bless them on that day, and here He commanded for all generations to Aaron and to his sons, and He specified the blessing that they shall bless them. And He mentioned it at the erection of the Tabernacle, for there HaShem appointed the blessing of life forever. And as our Sages said (Sotah 37): In the Sanctuary with the explicit Name, and in the provinces with its appellation; in the Sanctuary they would recite it as one blessing, and in the outlying regions as three blessings, for the blessing in the Sanctuary is uniquely designated with the unique Name:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The citation from Sotah 37 refers to b. Sotah 38a in standard editions; Ramban cites by chapter/daf number."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:02.959137098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}